<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zakarids</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–14th centuries</span> · Also known as Mkhargrdzeli, Zakarid dynasty, Zakarian dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zakarids, or Mkhargrdzeli, were an Armenian noble family who served the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> as commanders. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a> the brothers Zakare and Ivane took Ani in 1199 and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> from the Shaddadids and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>, ruling it as Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>. From the 1230s they became vassals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zakarids.jpg" alt="Zakarids" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Beko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holy_Mother_of_God_church_in_Geghard_-_details_01.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
